  "scope": "Unchanged Prayer, PrayerType, PrayerCategory, SkillBonus, Audio and PrayerTabInterface on JDK 11 with Kotlin 1.8.20 and the published ConstLib 1.4.28 (Sounds and Components; the bundled ConstLib-1.4.jar lacks the prayer sound names). Original text inserted into adapters at generation time: Skills.getStaticLevel, getPrayerPoints, decrementPrayerPoints, setPrayerPoints, heal, getMaximumLifepoints and the skill constants; Player.hasProtectionPrayer, commenceDeath and fullRestore; NPC.hasProtectionPrayer; Entity.getFormattedHit and isIgnoreProtection; ContentAPI hasLevelStat and setVarp; StringUtils.formatDisplayName; RandomFunction random and randomize; the Location packing, transform, withinDistance and getDistance; the ImpactHandler.HitsplatType enum; the CombatStyle protection prayers and ArmourSet constant names; the PrayerActivatedEvent/PrayerDeactivatedEvent declarations. Everything else is a recording adapter answering from the case: dispatch, appearance head icon and sync, audio, dialogue, King's Ransom requirement, varbit 3909, the pulse runner (queued pulses fire when the case asks), messages, bonuses, skillcape perks, graphics, locations, projectiles, manualHit, multi-zone, local entities, isAttackable, isPlaying, the superclass commenceDeath/fullRestore and the two Settings energy setters. RandomFunction.RANDOM is a seeded java.util.Random. Not driven: prayer training (bones, altars), SkillRestore's event hooks, DeathTask.getContainers (PROTECT_ITEMS), getDragonfireProtection, finalizeDeath, reentrant dispatch hooks and the real CombatSwingHandler/ImpactHandler (their own corpora drive them).",
